# Robin's settings, and what each one does. These are ENVIRONMENT
# VARIABLES — Robin does not read a .env file, so export them (or put
# them in the unit file / compose service that starts it).
#
# NEVER put an API key in here, or in any file you might commit.
#
# Keys are FILES, one per key name, read at call time:
#     mkdir -p ~/.robin-secrets && chmod 700 ~/.robin-secrets
#     printf '%s' "<your-key>" > ~/.robin-secrets/ARK_API_KEY
#     chmod 600 ~/.robin-secrets/ARK_API_KEY
#
# The file NAME is what llm_providers.json's `api_key_env` points at. Files
# rather than environment variables on purpose: an environment variable is
# inherited by every subprocess, and it lands in `docker inspect`, crash
# dumps and `ps` output. A file is read only when a call needs it.
#
# A key name with no file simply means "I do not hold this plan" — Robin skips
# that endpoint instead of burning a call that cannot succeed. (Give a no-auth
# local endpoint a placeholder file with any content: OpenAI clients refuse to
# start with no key at all.)

# ── The key files for the shipped examples ────────────────────────────────
# `api_key_env` in llm_providers.json names the FILE, so these are the names
# the shipped llm_providers.example.json asks for:
#
#     ARK_API_KEY        Volcengine Ark token plan   (ark/deepseek-v4-*)
#     GO_API_KEY         OpenCode Go subscription    (opencodego/deepseek-v4-*)
#     DEEPSEEK_API_KEY   DeepSeek pay-as-you-go      (the fallback tail)
#
#     mkdir -p ~/.robin-secrets && chmod 700 ~/.robin-secrets
#     printf '%s' "<ark key>"      > ~/.robin-secrets/ARK_API_KEY
#     printf '%s' "<opencode key>" > ~/.robin-secrets/GO_API_KEY
#     printf '%s' "<deepseek key>" > ~/.robin-secrets/DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
#     chmod 600 ~/.robin-secrets/*
#
# Hold only one of them? Create only that file. Robin skips the endpoints
# whose key is missing — the absence IS the configuration. Adding a fourth
# plan is a new provider entry plus a new file; no code, no restart of
# anything but Robin.
#
# Two plans with the SAME vendor: register the vendor twice under different
# names (`ark`, `ark2`) with different api_key_env (`ARK_API_KEY`,
# `ARK2_API_KEY`) and list both in the rotate pool. The spent-window cooldown
# keys on provider/model, so the two plans park independently.

# Where the key files live.
# ROBIN_SECRETS_DIR=~/.robin-secrets

# Where to listen. Loopback by default: Robin holds every key you own, so it
# must not be reachable from your network unless you put auth in front of it.
# ROBIN_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ROBIN_PORT=8080

# The two tables. Relative paths resolve against the working directory.
# ROBIN_PROVIDERS=llm_providers.json
# ROBIN_ROUTES=model_routes.json

# Optional: an API key clients must present to Robin itself (Authorization:
# Bearer <this>). Unset means no check — fine on loopback, not otherwise.
# ROBIN_API_KEY_FILE=~/.robin-secrets/ROBIN_API_KEY
